---

<LessonPage page={page}>
<main class="wrap" data-core-duration="70–80 minutes" data-extension-duration="15–20 minutes">
  <p class="kicker"><span class="dot"></span> Grammar · Lesson 7</p>
  <h1><em>Wish</em> and <em>if only</em>: locate reality before expressing distance</h1>
  <p class="standfirst">A wish compares reality with a preferred alternative. The grammar moves away from reality, but the form called “past” does not always mean past time. First locate the real situation. Then choose whether you want a different state now, unavailable ability now, a different completed past, or a change in behavior.</p>
  <div class="meta-row">
    <span class="tag">70–80 min core</span>
    <span class="tag">reality → preferred alternative</span>
    <span class="tag">past form, precise time</span>
    <span class="tag">15–20 min listening and retrieval</span>
  </div>

  <div class="lesson-flow" aria-label="Lesson flow">
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Locate</b><span>Is the real fact present, past, or still open?</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Choose</b><span>State, ability, regret, or desired change?</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Build</b><span>Keep every auxiliary and participle.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Respond</b><span>Express emotion without turning hindsight into blame.</span></div>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line"><b>Can-do:</b> By the end, you can use <span class="ex">wish / if only + Past Simple</span> for an unreal present, <span class="ex">could</span> for unavailable present ability, Past Perfect for past regret, and <span class="ex">would</span> for desired change; distinguish <span class="ex">wish</span> from an open future <span class="ex">hope</span> and formal <span class="ex">wish to</span>; choose <span class="ex">were</span> or natural informal <span class="ex">was</span> without a false absolute rule; hear contracted <span class="ex">’d</span> and reduced auxiliaries in U.S. speech; and turn a regret into a responsible next step.</p>

  <h2>Two-minute retrieval</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You recovered present counterfactual distance, Past Perfect, modal-perfect form, and two participles before using them inside wishes.">
    <h3>Reactivate the counterfactual foundation</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Wish foundation choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="were">were</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="had tested">had tested</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="might have found">might have found</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="sent">sent</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="known">known</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="would test">would test</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>If the room <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="were" data-hint="The room is not larger now. Use the counterfactual Past Simple form of be." data-fix="If the room were larger, we could add ten seats.">choose</button> larger, we could add ten seats.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>If the team <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="had tested" data-hint="The testing opportunity ended before launch, so build Past Perfect." data-fix="If the team had tested the older phones, it might have found the problem.">choose</button> the older phones, it <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="might have found" data-hint="Keep the past result uncertain with modal plus have plus participle." data-fix="It might have found the problem.">choose</button> the problem.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The past participle of <span class="ex">send</span> is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="sent" data-hint="The irregular form is the same in Past Simple and as the participle." data-fix="send → sent → sent">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The past participle of <span class="ex">know</span> is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="known" data-hint="Past Simple is knew, but the participle after had is different." data-fix="know → knew → known">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice: one project, four distances from reality</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Fictional Pine Street Learning Center open day</h3>
    <p><b>Current and recorded facts:</b> The main room holds 60 people, but 74 people registered. A second room is unavailable during a scheduled electrical inspection. Before registration opened, the team tested the form on desktop computers but not on three older phones. On launch day, 43 people tried the form on those phones, and 18 did not complete registration. The reminder system sent duplicate messages at 8:00 and 8:05 this morning. The vendor is working on a fix and still expects to finish by noon.</p>
    <p><span class="ex">I wish the main room were larger.</span> It is not larger now.</p>
    <p><span class="ex">I wish we could use the second room.</span> We cannot use it during the inspection.</p>
    <p><span class="ex">If only we had tested those phones before launch.</span> We did not test them, and that opportunity is over.</p>
    <p><span class="ex">I wish the reminder system would stop sending duplicates.</span> The speaker wants a repeated, changeable process to stop.</p>
    <p><span class="ex">I hope the vendor finishes by noon.</span> Noon is still in the future, so success remains possible.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You matched each sentence to the real time and the speaker's intended attitude before naming the form.">
    <h3>Discovery check: recover reality and attitude</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Wish discovery choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="an unreal present state">an unreal present state</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="unavailable present ability">unavailable present ability</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="regret about a completed past">regret about a completed past</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="a desired change in a repeated process">a desired change in a repeated process</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="an open future possibility">an open future possibility</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="emotional emphasis, not a new time pattern">emotional emphasis, not a new time pattern</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span><span class="ex">I wish the room were larger</span> presents <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="an unreal present state" data-hint="Compare the preferred size with the room's actual size now." data-fix="The room is not larger now, so the sentence presents an unreal present state.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span><span class="ex">I wish we could use the second room</span> presents <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="unavailable present ability" data-hint="The inspection prevents use now." data-fix="Could marks an ability or possibility that is unavailable now.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span><span class="ex">If only we had tested those phones</span> presents <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="regret about a completed past" data-hint="The registration launch has already happened." data-fix="Past Perfect creates an alternative to a completed past fact.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span><span class="ex">I wish the system would stop</span> presents <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="a desired change in a repeated process" data-hint="Duplicate messages keep happening, and the process can change." data-fix="Would asks for a repeated, changeable process to behave differently.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span><span class="ex">I hope the vendor finishes by noon</span> presents <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="an open future possibility" data-hint="Noon has not arrived, and the fix may still happen." data-fix="Hope fits a future outcome that remains genuinely possible.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>Compared with <span class="ex">wish</span>, <span class="ex">if only</span> commonly adds <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="emotional emphasis, not a new time pattern" data-hint="Both expressions can use Past Simple, Past Perfect, could, or would according to meaning." data-fix="If only can intensify longing, frustration, or regret, but the time relationship still selects the form.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Get to the root: map real time, preferred reality, and attitude</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>The past-looking form marks <b>distance from reality</b>. Real time still matters because the distance can point away from a present fact or back toward a completed past. <span class="ex">Would</span> adds a desired change, while <span class="ex">could</span> focuses on unavailable ability or possibility.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Meaning</th><th>Core pattern</th><th>Reality</th><th>Preferred alternative</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>different present state</td><td>wish / if only + <b>Past Simple</b></td><td>The room is small.</td><td>I wish it <b>were larger</b>.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>unavailable present ability</td><td>wish / if only + <b>could + base</b></td><td>We cannot use Room B.</td><td>I wish we <b>could use</b> it.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>different completed past</td><td>wish / if only + <b>Past Perfect</b></td><td>We did not test the phones.</td><td>If only we <b>had tested</b> them.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>desired behavior or process change</td><td>wish / if only + subject + <b>would + base</b></td><td>The system keeps sending duplicates.</td><td>I wish it <b>would stop</b>.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="note">
    <h3><span class="ex">Were</span>, <span class="ex">was</span>, and a useful standard target</h3>
    <p>Counterfactual <span class="ex">were</span> is available with every subject: <span class="ex">I wish I were there</span> and <span class="ex">If only the room were larger</span>. It is a dependable target in careful professional and academic English. <span class="ex">Was</span> also occurs naturally with <span class="ex">I, he, she,</span> and <span class="ex">it</span> in informal U.S. conversation. Do not describe every informal <span class="ex">I wish I was</span> as impossible. Use <span class="ex">were</span> when you want an unambiguously counterfactual careful form.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. Every choice now follows the stated real time and attitude instead of the word wish alone.">
    <h3>Choose nine meaning-time relationships</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Wish meaning and time choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="lived">lived</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="could attend">could attend</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="had saved">had saved</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="would lower">would lower</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="were">were</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="hadn't sent">hadn't sent</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="wouldn't interrupt">wouldn't interrupt</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="could stay">could stay</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="had known">had known</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="will finish">will finish</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>My apartment is far from work now. I wish I <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="lived" data-hint="This is a different present state, not a past residence." data-fix="I wish I lived closer to work.">choose</button> closer to work.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The conference is today, but my schedule makes attendance impossible. I wish I <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="could attend" data-hint="Focus on unavailable ability today." data-fix="I wish I could attend the conference.">choose</button> the conference.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>We deleted the only local copy last night. If only we <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="had saved" data-hint="The saving opportunity ended before the deletion." data-fix="If only we had saved a backup.">choose</button> a backup.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The ventilation fan keeps making a loud tone, and maintenance can change its setting. I wish they <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="would lower" data-hint="The speaker wants another party to change a controllable setting." data-fix="I wish they would lower the fan speed.">choose</button> the fan speed.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The office is not quieter now. In careful English: I wish it <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="were" data-hint="Use the careful counterfactual form of be for an unreal present." data-fix="I wish it were quieter.">choose</button> quieter.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>I sent a rushed reply yesterday and now regret it. I wish I <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="hadn't sent" data-hint="Negate the completed past action inside Past Perfect." data-fix="I wish I hadn't sent the reply so quickly.">choose</button> the reply so quickly.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">7</span><span>My coworker repeatedly speaks over clients, and I want that behavior to change. If only he <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="wouldn't interrupt" data-hint="This is a complaint about another person's repeated, potentially controllable behavior." data-fix="If only he wouldn't interrupt clients.">choose</button> clients.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">8</span><span>The last train leaves in five minutes, so we cannot remain for the final question. We wish we <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="could stay" data-hint="The current schedule removes the ability to stay." data-fix="We wish we could stay for the final question.">choose</button> for the final question.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">9</span><span>The deadline passed before I learned about the grant. If only I <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="had known" data-hint="The knowing needed to happen before a completed deadline." data-fix="If only I had known about the grant earlier.">choose</button> about the grant earlier.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Build the complete clause, not a tense label</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Function</th><th>Form after wish / if only</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>present positive alternative</td><td>subject + Past Simple</td><td>I wish the form <b>worked</b>.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>present negative alternative</td><td>subject + did not + base</td><td>I wish it <b>didn't require</b> two steps.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>present state with be</td><td>subject + were / informal was</td><td>If only the room <b>were available</b>.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>unavailable ability</td><td>subject + could not / could + base</td><td>I wish we <b>could move</b> upstairs.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>past positive alternative</td><td>subject + had + participle</td><td>I wish we <b>had tested</b> it.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>past negative alternative</td><td>subject + had not + participle</td><td>I wish we <b>hadn't opened</b> registration yet.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>desired positive change</td><td>subject + would + base</td><td>I wish the vendor <b>would reply</b>.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>desired negative change</td><td>subject + would not + base</td><td>I wish the system <b>wouldn't resend</b> notices.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="note">
    <h3>Questions ask about the whole wish</h3>
    <p>In <span class="ex">What do you wish you had known?</span>, <span class="ex">do you wish</span> carries question order. The embedded preferred reality keeps statement order: <span class="ex">you had known</span>, not <span class="ex">had you known</span>. In <span class="ex">Do you wish the schedule were different?</span>, do not invert the embedded subject and verb.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You kept statement order inside the wish and retained every auxiliary, negative, base verb, and participle.">
    <h3>Complete ten form decisions</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Wish form choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="worked">worked</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="didn't require">didn't require</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="were available">were available</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="could move">could move</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="had tested">had tested</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="hadn't opened">hadn't opened</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="would reply">would reply</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="wouldn't resend">wouldn't resend</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="you had known">you had known</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="the schedule were">the schedule were</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="you knew">you knew</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The form fails on my phone now. I wish it <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="worked" data-hint="Use Past Simple for a preferred present state." data-fix="I wish it worked on my phone.">choose</button> on my phone.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The current process requires two approvals. I wish it <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="didn't require" data-hint="Use did not plus the base verb for the negative present alternative." data-fix="I wish it didn't require two approvals.">choose</button> two approvals.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>Room B is unavailable today. If only it <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="were available" data-hint="Keep counterfactual were plus the complement." data-fix="If only it were available today.">choose</button> today.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The inspection prevents us from moving upstairs. I wish we <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="could move" data-hint="Could is followed by the base verb." data-fix="I wish we could move upstairs.">choose</button> upstairs.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>We did not test three older phones before launch. I wish we <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="had tested" data-hint="Build Past Perfect with had plus the participle." data-fix="I wish we had tested the three older phones.">choose</button> the three older phones.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>Registration already opened with an incorrect capacity. If only we <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="hadn't opened" data-hint="Put not after had and retain the participle opened." data-fix="If only we hadn't opened registration yet.">choose</button> registration yet.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">7</span><span>The vendor has not answered three status requests. I wish the vendor <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="would reply" data-hint="The speaker wants another party to change a repeated pattern of nonresponse." data-fix="I wish the vendor would reply.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">8</span><span>The system repeatedly sends a second notice. I wish it <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="wouldn't resend" data-hint="Use would not plus the base verb for the unwanted repeated process." data-fix="I wish it wouldn't resend the notice.">choose</button> the notice.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">9</span><span>What do you wish <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="you had known" data-hint="The question order is in do you wish; keep statement order inside the embedded past regret." data-fix="What do you wish you had known before launch?">choose</button> before launch?</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">10</span><span>Do you wish <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="the schedule were" data-hint="Keep the embedded subject before the counterfactual verb." data-fix="Do you wish the schedule were different?">choose</button> different?</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Keep nearby meanings separate</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="note">
    <h3><span class="ex">Wish</span>, <span class="ex">hope</span>, and formal <span class="ex">wish to</span></h3>
    <ul>
      <li><span class="ex">I hope the vendor finishes by noon</span> treats the future result as open and possible.</li>
      <li><span class="ex">I wish the vendor had finished by noon yesterday</span> creates an alternative to a completed past fact.</li>
      <li><span class="ex">I wish to speak with the coordinator</span> is a formal way to say <span class="ex">I want to speak</span>. It is not the counterfactual pattern in this lesson.</li>
      <li>A noun can follow <span class="ex">wish</span> in conventional expressions: <span class="ex">We wish you a safe trip</span>.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="note">
    <h3>Use <span class="ex">would</span> for a plausible desired change, not every dissatisfaction</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><span class="ex">I wish the alarm would stop</span> asks for a current process to change.</li>
      <li><span class="ex">I wish my coworker would listen</span> asks another person to change potentially controllable behavior.</li>
      <li>For a stable present state, prefer Past Simple: <span class="ex">I wish the office were closer</span>, not <span class="ex">would be closer</span>.</li>
      <li>For your own current knowledge or stable characteristic, prefer Past Simple: <span class="ex">I wish I knew</span>. <span class="ex">I wish I would know</span> does not express this meaning.</li>
      <li>Speakers can use <span class="ex">would</span> with their own future willingness or recurring behavior in special self-critical contexts, but do not use that marked pattern as a general replacement for <span class="ex">I wish I could</span> or <span class="ex">I wish I were</span>.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="note">
    <h3><span class="ex">I wish I could have attended</span> versus <span class="ex">I wish I had attended</span></h3>
    <p>Both can concern a past event. <span class="ex">I wish I had attended</span> directly regrets nonattendance. <span class="ex">I wish I could have attended</span> highlights that attendance was not possible or available. State the obstacle if that distinction matters: <span class="ex">I wish I could have attended, but my flight was canceled.</span></p>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You distinguished counterfactual wishes from open hope, formal want, stable states, desired change, and unavailable past opportunity.">
    <h3>Choose ten boundary meanings from full contexts</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Wish boundary choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="hope">hope</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="wish">wish</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="wish to">wish to</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="wish you">wish you</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="were">were</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="would stop">would stop</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="knew">knew</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="could attend">could attend</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="had attended">had attended</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="could have attended">could have attended</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="will stop">will stop</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The vendor is still working, and noon is two hours away. We <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="hope" data-hint="The future result is still genuinely possible." data-fix="We hope the vendor finishes by noon.">choose</button> the vendor finishes by noon.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The vendor missed yesterday's noon deadline. We <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="wish" data-hint="The completed past fact is now different from the preferred reality." data-fix="We wish the vendor had finished by noon yesterday.">choose</button> the vendor had finished by noon yesterday.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>In a formal service email, <span class="ex">I <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="wish to" data-hint="Here wish means formally want, so it is followed by to plus base verb." data-fix="I wish to request a corrected invoice.">choose</button> request a corrected invoice</span> means I formally want to request one.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>Before a friend's trip, <span class="ex">We <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="wish you" data-hint="This is the conventional wish plus person plus noun pattern." data-fix="We wish you a safe trip.">choose</button> a safe trip</span> does not describe an unreal situation.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The building is permanently far from the station. I wish it <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="were" data-hint="Use Past Simple for a stable unreal present state." data-fix="I wish it were closer to the station.">choose</button> closer to the station.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>A temporary alarm has sounded for ten minutes, and maintenance can reset it. I wish it <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="would stop" data-hint="This is a current changeable process the speaker wants to end." data-fix="I wish it would stop.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">7</span><span>I do not know the code now. I wish I <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="knew" data-hint="Knowledge is a present state, not desired future willingness." data-fix="I wish I knew the code.">choose</button> the code.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">8</span><span>The workshop is happening now, but my shift makes attendance impossible. I wish I <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="could attend" data-hint="Focus on unavailable present ability." data-fix="I wish I could attend the workshop.">choose</button> the workshop.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">9</span><span>I freely chose not to attend yesterday, and now I regret the choice. I wish I <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="had attended" data-hint="The focus is the completed nonattendance itself, not an external obstacle." data-fix="I wish I had attended yesterday.">choose</button> yesterday.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">10</span><span>I wanted to attend yesterday, but my canceled flight made it impossible. I wish I <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="could have attended" data-hint="Highlight the unavailable past opportunity and keep modal plus have plus participle." data-fix="I wish I could have attended, but my flight was canceled.">choose</button>.</span></div>
